<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bato of Dardania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bato was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dardanians">Dardani</a>, son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/longarus">Longarus</a>, who ruled in the late 3rd century BCE. In 200 BCE, at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-macedonian-war">Second Macedonian War</a>, he offered help to the Roman consul Publius Sulpicius Galba against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a>, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> records. The alliance reflected the Dardanians' long hostility to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, their southern neighbour.</p></div>
